cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  "If you use this software and the accompanying study, please cite version
  5.0.0. v5.0.0 corrects misleading temperature claims of earlier versions and
  adds an electrostatic-selectivity analysis; earlier versions should not be
  cited as evidence."
type: software
title: "EQLI / Entangletronica: Electrostatic Quantum-Lens Interferometry in InGaAs 2DEGs"
version: "5.0.0"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible split-step Schrodinger simulations of a single flying electron
  through a gate-defined double-slit interferometer in a ballistic 2DEG, with a
  programmable electrostatic phase lens, a Poisson-Thomas-Fermi voltage mapping,
  a conservative white-noise dephasing budget, a stochastic-dephasing ensemble,
  and a correlated-noise check. Companion to the EQLI preprint.

  Honest scope: this is a numerical model, not an experiment — no experimental
  data are included. The operating temperature bound T_max ~ 11 K is a
  conservative worst case for white noise (rising to ~29 K for spatially
  correlated noise), and the single-electron-transistor (SET) readout at
  T < 1 K is the practical thermal bottleneck, not the coherence bound. The
  electrostatic differential-selectivity ratio is ~0.69; the 50 meV/V
  amplitude and the dephasing scale s_phi = 22 are empirical calibration
  (consistency) parameters, not first-principles predictions.
authors:
